T*
(9. Verification Results) Tj
T*
(- Tesseract executable found: Yes) Tj
T*
(- Core Python dependencies found: Yes) Tj
T*
(- Pytest result: 34 tests passed) Tj
T*
(- Backend sample pipeline run: Success in offline fallback mode) Tj
T*
(- FastAPI route structure: Present) Tj
T*
(- Frontend build: Failed locally) Tj
T*
(- LLM runtime check: Integrated but not operational now) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(10. Benchmark Note) Tj
T*
(The existing benchmark_results.csv file shows mixed OCR quality.) Tj
T*
(One sample scored about 56.25 percent, another 10.53 percent, mixed text 37.5 percent,) Tj
T*
(and Tamil samples 0 percent. This shows the project idea is working, but OCR quality and) Tj
T*
(Tamil handling still need improvement.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(11. Final Conclusion) Tj
T*
(BrailleAir is a meaningful project with a clear goal. It already has a full processing) Tj
T*
(pipeline,) Tj
T*
(a web API, a frontend, a Braille encoding layer, and optional AI integration.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The project is partially working.) Tj
T*
(The offline core demo works in a basic form.) Tj
T*
(The online structure exists, but it is not fully reliable in the current environment.) Tj
T*
(The LLM is integrated, but it is not working correctly now.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(In simple words:) Tj
T*
(BrailleAir is a good working prototype, not a finished production-ready system.) Tj
T*
ET
